{{define "before"}}## Before you start

1. Sign in to Colliedesk and open **Settings → External AI agents**.
2. Name the token (for example "{{.Host.Name}} on my laptop"), choose what it may do (follow one of your
   roles, or pick permissions; leaving out sending to customers is a good start) and choose **Create token**.
   See [Agent tokens](sessions.md#agent-tokens).
3. Copy the token. It starts with `{{.TokenPrefix}}` and is shown once.

The steps below use `{{.Origin}}`: put the address you open Colliedesk at in its place.
Under **Connect your agent**, Settings shows these steps for {{.Host.Name}} with your address already in.
{{end}}

{{define "try"}}## Try it

Ask {{.Host.Name}}: "Who am I in Colliedesk?" It calls `colliedesk_whoami`, which answers
with your name, your workspace, your roles, the token's permissions and the tools it may use. Then, for example: "Triage the
open conversations nobody owns: tag billing questions with `billing` and leave a note with a
summary."
{{end}}

{{define "access"}}## What the agent can do

Colliedesk has {{.Tools}} tools. The agent acts as you, with the permissions you gave the token,
never more than you hold now. A tool it has the permissions for runs at once; any other is refused
with the permission it lacks. See [Roles and permissions](roles-and-permissions.md).

Every tool and what it needs: [Connect an AI agent (MCP)](mcp.md#tools).
{{end}}

{{define "revoke"}}Then revoke the token in **Settings → Sessions**: it stops working at once, wherever it was
copied.
{{end}}

